Based on the context documents provided, when a streaming resume attempt fails with HTTP 409 (checkpoint mismatch), the server's error payload includes the following JSON schema:

```json
{
  "title": "Streaming Error Payload",
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "error": {
      "type": "object",
      "properties": {
        "code": {
          "type": "integer",
          "minimum": 0
        },
        "message": {
          "type": "string"
        }
      }
    },
    "resume_details": {
      "type": "object",
      "properties": {
        "resume_token": {
          "type": "string"
        },
        "checkpoint_sequence": {
          "type": "integer"
        },
        "kv_crc": {
          "type": "string"
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
```

The `kv_crc` value inside v2 resume tokens is computed as a cyclic redundancy check (CRC) of the key-value pair in the resume token. The CRC algorithm used is not specified in the context documents provided.
